---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Infinite Ruler Support — Savoie Apps"
  description="Calibration, measurement and troubleshooting help for Infinite Ruler."
  canonicalUrl="https://savoie.app/apps/infinite-ruler/support/"
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="app-info">
    <article class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Infinite Ruler</p>
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="lede">Need help with calibration, fractional inches, movable zero, A–B markers or measuring beyond one screen? Email us and we’ll help you get it sorted.</p>

      <a class="contact" href="mailto:infinite-ruler@savoie.app?subject=Infinite%20Ruler%20Support%20Request">Email Infinite Ruler support</a>

      <h2>Helpful details to include</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your Infinite Ruler version and build number</li>
        <li>Your iPhone model and iOS version</li>
        <li>What you expected to happen and what happened instead</li>
        <li>A screenshot, if it helps explain the problem</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Common fixes</h2>
      <h3>The scale does not match a physical ruler</h3>
      <p>Open calibration from the ruler controls and adjust the scale against a trusted physical ruler. Device profiles provide a starting point, but calibration is recommended for accuracy-sensitive work.</p>

      <h3>I need to start away from the phone edge</h3>
      <p>Press and hold the orange zero briefly. When you feel the haptic, drag it to the point where you want the measurement to begin.</p>

      <h3>I want the distance between two points</h3>
      <p>Show the measurement markers, then touch the ruler at point A and drag to point B. Infinite Ruler displays the distance between them using your selected unit and precision.</p>

      <h3>The object is longer than the screen</h3>
      <p>Use the next and previous controls to continue the ruler scale page by page without losing your accumulated position.</p>

      <p class="footnote">Infinite Ruler is intended for convenient everyday measurements. Calibrate against a physical ruler before work that requires greater accuracy. See the <a href="/apps/infinite-ruler/privacy/">Infinite Ruler privacy policy</a> for data-handling details.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .app-info { padding: 4rem 0 5rem; }
  .app-info .container { max-width: 720px; }
  .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 .5rem; color: #0a84ff; font-weight: 700; }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 7vw, 3.75rem); letter-spacing: -.05em; }
  .lede { max-width: 42rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: 1.12rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .contact { display: inline-block; margin: 1rem 0 2rem; padding: .8rem 1rem; border-radius: .8rem; background: #0a84ff; color: white; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; }
  h2 { margin: 2rem 0 .7rem; font-size: 1.3rem; }
  h3 { margin: 1.4rem 0 .35rem; font-size: 1rem; }
  p, li { line-height: 1.7; }
  li + li { margin-top: .35rem; }
  .footnote { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: .9rem; }
</style>
